# UI Components Formalization Plan

**Goal:** Formalize and consolidate reusable UI widgets/components into
`AgentFoundation/src/agent_foundation/ui` so that downstream applications
(OpenStartup, RankEvolve, future agent UIs) consume a single, well-defined
component library instead of forking and diverging.

**Author:** Drafted via deep cross-codebase investigation, 2026-05-23.
**Status:** PROPOSED — awaiting sign-off before execution.

---

## 0. TL;DR

1. **Three codebases** all carry copies of essentially the same "agent
   interaction widget set" (TextInput / SingleChoice / MultipleChoice /
   Confirmation / etc.) plus a small set of pure-UI primitives
   (LoadingIndicator, MarkdownRenderer, PersonChip, StatusBadge, …).
2. **AgentFoundation already has** a widget protocol (Python
   `widget_protocol.py` + a React `webui/react/src/components/widgets/`
   registry) — it is the **natural home** for the canonical components.
3. **OpenStartup** and **RankEvolve** today **fork-and-diverge** from
   AgentFoundation's UI; OpenStartup even documents this in
   `shared/index.js` ("Adapted from AgentFoundation/.../components/common/").
4. We propose a **5-phase formalization**:
   Phase 1 — Inventory & freeze (no behavioral change).
   Phase 2 — Promote pure primitives into AgentFoundation `ui/widgets/common/`.
   Phase 3 — Canonicalize the **widget protocol** components in
   `ui/widgets/inputs/` (TextInput, SingleChoice, MultipleChoice,
   Confirmation, Dropdown, Toggle, ToolArgumentForm, MultiInput,
   Default) and register them via a single `WidgetRegistry` source of truth.
   Phase 4 — Publish a consumable package (`@agent-foundation/ui-react`
   workspace + Python entry-point loader) and migrate OpenStartup &
   RankEvolve to consume it.
   Phase 5 — Set up contribution rules, lint guards, and a visual snapshot
   test harness so divergence cannot silently reappear.

The plan deliberately **keeps domain-specific widgets** (ProjectSummary,
SprintProgress, TaskAssignment, WorkloadChart, ProposalSelection, Hub,
Pipeline*) in their respective apps. Only the **generic, agent-protocol-
shaped** components move.

---

## 1. Investigation Findings

### 1.1 Codebases & Roles

| Codebase | Path | Role |
|----------|------|------|
| AgentFoundation | `CoreProjects/AgentFoundation/src/agent_foundation/ui/` | The **framework**. Owns Python `interactive_base`, `input_modes`, `widget_protocol`, and the canonical React `webui/`. |
| OpenStartup (OpenTEAM) | `CoreProjects/OpenStartup/src/openteam/ui/` | A **product UI** built on top of MUI 7 + React 19. Imports from local copies that were "Adapted from" AgentFoundation. |
| RankEvolve | `CoreProjects/atlassian-packages/rankevolve/src/webui/` | An **independent application** of the framework. Lives in a separate package; today is the *de facto* upstream from which AgentFoundation's `webui/` was forked. |

### 1.2 Key files that already exist in AgentFoundation

**Python protocol layer** (authoritative):

- `ui/widget_protocol.py` — `WidgetMessage`, `WidgetResponse`, `WidgetField`,
  `WIDGET_TEXT_INPUT`, `WIDGET_SINGLE_CHOICE`, `WIDGET_MULTIPLE_CHOICE`,
  `WIDGET_DROPDOWN`, `WIDGET_TOGGLE`, `WIDGET_TOOL_ARGUMENT_FORM`.
- `ui/input_modes.py` — `InputMode` StrEnum (`FREE_TEXT`,
  `PRESS_TO_CONTINUE`, `EXACT_STRING`, `SINGLE_CHOICE`, `MULTIPLE_CHOICE`),
  `InputModeConfig`, `ChoiceOption`, plus convenience constructors
  (`press_to_continue`, `exact_string`, `single_choice`,
  `multiple_choices`).
- `ui/interactive_base.py`, `ui/rich_interactive_base.py`,
  `ui/terminal_interactive.py`, `ui/queue_interactive.py`,
  `ui/email_interactive.py`, `ui/simulated_interactive.py` —
  back-end implementations of the interactive protocol.
- `ui/dash_interactive/` — Python-only Dash app (separate UI surface;
  out of scope for this plan but referenced).

**React layer (already present, but currently a fork of RankEvolve)**:

- `ui/webui/react/src/components/widgets/` — WidgetRegistry +
  TextInput / SingleChoice / MultipleChoice / Confirmation / Dropdown /
  Toggle / ToolArgumentForm / MultiInput / Default / ToolConfigPanel.
- `ui/webui/react/src/components/common/` — ClickToEditMarkdown,
  EmptyState, LoadingIndicator, MarkdownRenderer, PersonChip,
  PlanModeSelector, ProgressBar, QuickLinkButton, SectionCard,
  StatusBadge, WelcomeScreen.
- `ui/webui/react/src/components/agent/` — AgentChatPanel,
  AgentStatusBar, AgentStreamDrawer, AgentStreamSection,
  CommandAutocomplete, SessionSidebar, StreamingMessage, TaskCard,
  TaskPanel.
- `ui/webui/react/src/components/chat|layout|progress|queries|messages|actions/`
- `ui/webui/react/src/hooks/` — useAgentChat, useAgentWebSocket,
  useChat, useContextMenu, useFileViewer, useInputFields, useProgress,
  useProgressHeader, useSectionVisibility, useSessionApi,
  useSessionManager, useWorkspace.
- `ui/webui/react/src/theme/` — createAppTheme, cssVariableBridge,
  ThemeProvider, themeRegistry, ThemeSwitcher (+ tests).
- `ui/webui/react/src/contexts/SessionContext.js`.
- `ui/webui/src/...` — an **older, partial duplicate** of the above
  (legacy). To be removed in Phase 1 cleanup.

### 1.3 The Divergence Problem (proven by `diff -rq`)

`AgentFoundation/.../webui/react/src/components/` differs from
`rankevolve/.../webui/react/src/components/` in essentially **every**
file that exists in both:

- `agent/AgentChatPanel.js` differs
- `agent/AgentStatusBar.js` differs
- `agent/AgentStreamDrawer.js` differs
- `agent/AgentStreamSection.js` differs
- `agent/CommandAutocomplete.js` differs
- `agent/SessionSidebar.js` differs
- `agent/StreamingMessage.js` differs
- `agent/TaskCard.js` differs
- `agent/TaskPanel.js` differs
- `common/ClickToEditMarkdown.js` differs
- `common/MarkdownRenderer.js` differs
- `common/PlanModeSelector.js` differs
- `common/index.js` differs
- `layout/AppHeader.js`, `layout/FileViewer.js` differ
- `progress/*.js` differs across the board
- `queries/AddDropdown.js`, `queries/AddQueriesDropdown.js`,
  `queries/QueryCard.js` differ
- `widgets/ConfirmationWidget.js`, `widgets/MultiInputWidget.js`,
  `widgets/SingleChoiceWidget.js`, `widgets/TextInputWidget.js`,
  `widgets/ToolConfigPanel.js`, `widgets/WidgetRegistry.js` differ
- RankEvolve **only**: `agent/MultiViewTaskPanel.js`,
  `agent/PipelineStatusBar.js`, `agent/ViewTabBar.js`,
  `common/SplitActionButton.js`, `widgets/GroupedWidget.js`,
  `widgets/ProposalSelectionWidget.js`, `components/hub/*`,
  `components/views/*`.
- AgentFoundation **only**: `common/EmptyState.js`,
  `common/PersonChip.js`, `common/ProgressBar.js`,
  `common/QuickLinkButton.js`, `common/SectionCard.js`,
  `common/StatusBadge.js`.

**Conclusion:** RankEvolve and AgentFoundation have **already** drifted.
OpenStartup independently reimplemented many of the same primitives
(`shared/EmptyState.js`, `shared/LoadingIndicator.js`,
`shared/PersonChip.js`, `shared/ProgressBar.js`,
`shared/QuickLinkButton.js`, `shared/SectionCard.js`,
`shared/StatusBadge.js`, `shared/PendingReasonPopover.js`) and built its
own widget set (`components/chat-widgets/`) with the *same* shape but
*different* code. This is the exact failure mode the formalization must
prevent going forward.

### 1.4 OpenStartup Inventory (`openteam/ui/src/`)

Built on **MUI 7** + React 19 + react-markdown + react-syntax-highlighter.
Uses a custom `theme.custom` namespace (`categorical`, `surfaces`).

**a) Pure UI primitives — `shared/`** — direct candidates for upstream
(file headers explicitly say "Adapted from AgentFoundation"):

| File | Status | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| `EmptyState.js` | DUPLICATES AF | AF already has `common/EmptyState.js` |
| `LoadingIndicator.js` | DUPLICATES AF | AF already has `common/LoadingIndicator.js` |
| `PendingReasonPopover.js` | **NEW** | Generic resolution popover; not in AF. Candidate for promotion. |
| `PersonChip.js` | DUPLICATES AF | AF already has `common/PersonChip.js` |
| `ProgressBar.js` | DUPLICATES AF | AF already has `common/ProgressBar.js` |
| `QuickLinkButton.js` | DUPLICATES AF | AF already has `common/QuickLinkButton.js` |
| `SectionCard.js` | DUPLICATES AF | AF already has `common/SectionCard.js` |
| `StatusBadge.js` | DUPLICATES AF | AF already has `common/StatusBadge.js` |

**b) Chat widgets — `components/chat-widgets/`** — split:

Generic (move to / reconcile with AF widgets):
- `WidgetRegistry.js` — overlaps AF's; AF version is more complete.
- `ChatWidgetRenderer.js` — generic registry dispatcher.
- `ConversationToolWidget.js` — generic `input_mode`-protocol dispatcher.
- `ConfirmationWidget.js`, `SingleChoiceWidget.js`,
  `MultipleChoiceWidget.js`, `TextInputWidget.js`,
  `ApprovalWidget.js`, `ChoiceWidget.js` — all schema-driven; all
  match the AF protocol.

Domain-specific (keep in OpenStartup):
- `ProjectSummaryWidget.js`, `SprintProgressWidget.js`,
  `TaskAssignmentWidget.js`, `TaskListWidget.js`,
  `WorkloadChartWidget.js`.

**c) Chat components — `components/chat/`** — split:

Generic candidates: `MarkdownRenderer.js` (overlaps AF + RE),
`StreamingMessage.js` (overlaps AF + RE), `Breadcrumb.js`,
`ThinkingFold.js`, `PromptViewerDrawer.js`, `NodeDetailPanel.js`,
`GraphFlowView.js`, `CommandAutocomplete.js` (overlaps AF + RE),
`BackendSelector.js`, `ChatInput.js` (overlaps AF + RE),
`AgentMessageBubble.js`.

OpenTEAM-specific: `SessionContextBar.js`, `TaskCard.js` (OpenTEAM
flavour), `TaskPanel.js` (OpenTEAM flavour).

**d) Layout — `components/layout/`** — `ConnectionStatusBar.js`
(generic), `FileViewer.js` (overlaps AF + RE), `FolderTree.js`
(generic candidate), `SettingsDrawer.js` (app-specific scaffold),
`Sidebar.js` (OpenTEAM session/task sidebar — keep in app).

**e) Hooks — `hooks/`** — `useApiData.js`, `useServerStatus.js`
(generic candidates). Others (`useFileViewer`, `useGraphState`,
`useManagerChat`, `usePromptViewer`, `useServerBackends`,
`useTaskTopologies`) are domain-specific.

**f) Theme — `theme/`** — `createAppTheme.js`, `cssVariableBridge.js`,
`ThemeProvider.js`, `themeRegistry.js`, `ThemeSwitcher.js`, plus three
theme definitions (`atlassian`, `dark`, `pinterest`). The
**implementation appears to be the same shape** as AF's theme system
but is currently independently maintained — strong consolidation
candidate.

**g) Domain components** (keep in app): `components/employees/*`,
`components/projects/*`, `components/tasks/*`, `components/teams/*`,
`components/views/*`.

### 1.5 RankEvolve Inventory (`rankevolve/src/webui/react/src/`)

Same MUI-based stack. Currently is the **de facto upstream** of the AF
`webui/` fork. Contains everything AF has, plus RE-specific extras:

- `components/hub/*` (HowCombosWork, ScriptEditorDrawer,
  SetupWizardModal, SubmissionActionButton, SubmissionFooterBar,
  SubmitExperimentConfirm, UploadExistingRunnerModal) — **RE domain**.
- `components/views/*` (AnalysisView, JobMonitorView,
  MultiChoiceComboView, QueueProgressView, RunQueueList, …) — **RE
  domain**.
- `widgets/GroupedWidget.js` — Plan v3 compound widget — **generic**
  pattern, suitable for promotion.
- `widgets/ProposalSelectionWidget.js` — **RE domain** (proposals).
- `agent/MultiViewTaskPanel.js`, `agent/PipelineStatusBar.js`,
  `agent/ViewTabBar.js` — Plan v3 multi-view experience —
  **RE-shaped** but the *pattern* (multi-task panel, pipeline status,
  view tab bar) is generic.
- `common/SplitActionButton.js` — generic primitive — promotion candidate.
- `hooks/` adds: `useArchiveCount`, `useAggregationSettings`,
  `useAutopilot`, `useComboOverrides`, `useHypothesisImplementations`,
  `useProposalOverrides`, `useSubmissionTemplates`,
  `useViewWorkspace`, `_autopilotChipFinders` — **RE domain**.
- `contexts/SessionContext.js` — extends AF's; has RE actions baked in.

### 1.6 AgentFoundation Existing Architecture (recap)

- Python `widget_protocol.py` and `input_modes.py` are the **contract**.
  Any UI in the ecosystem must speak this dict shape.
- React `webui/react/src/components/widgets/WidgetRegistry.js`
  currently handles: `text_input`, `free_text`, `single_choice`,
  `multiple_choice`, `multiple_choices`, `dropdown`, `toggle`,
  `confirmation`, `tool_argument_form`, `multi_input`, `default`.
  This matches the Python constants 1:1.
- React `webui/react/src/components/common/` is the **only place**
  today that holds `EmptyState`, `PersonChip`, `ProgressBar`,
  `QuickLinkButton`, `SectionCard`, `StatusBadge` — these are
  duplicated downstream as `shared/*` in OpenStartup.
- `webui/src/` (older variant) is **dead code** and should be removed.
- `webui/` is structured as a **bundled application** today (it has its
  own `run_server.sh`, `backend/`, `package.json`, etc.), not as a
  consumable library. This is the biggest architectural gap.

