### 2.2 Contracts

The library exposes **three stable contracts** that downstream apps
program against. Versioning is semver, with the Python `widget_protocol`
constants being the source of truth.

**Contract 1 — Widget data shape (transport).**
Mirrors `widget_protocol.WidgetMessage.to_dict()`:

```ts
type WidgetMessage = {
  widget_id: string;
  widget_type:
    | 'text_input' | 'free_text'
    | 'single_choice' | 'multiple_choice' | 'multiple_choices'
    | 'dropdown' | 'toggle' | 'confirmation'
    | 'tool_argument_form' | 'multi_input' | 'grouped'
    | 'approval' | 'choice' | 'press_to_continue' | 'default';
  title?: string;
  description?: string;
  input_mode?: InputModeConfigDict;
  fields?: WidgetFieldDict[];
  metadata?: Record<string, any>;
};

type WidgetResponse = {
  widget_id: string;
  values: Record<string, any>;
  action: 'submit' | 'cancel' | 'skip';
};
```

**Contract 2 — React component prop shape.**
Every input widget MUST accept exactly:

```ts
type WidgetProps = {
  widget: WidgetMessage;            // immutable; never mutated by widget
  onSubmit: (r: WidgetResponse) => void;
  onCancel?: () => void;
  // Optional cross-cutting concerns:
  onView?: (path: string) => void;       // open file viewer
  onViewFolder?: (path: string) => void; // open folder tree
  disabled?: boolean;
};
```

This is intentionally narrower than the current RE/AF/OS variants
(which leak `config`, `data`, and `pendingInput` shapes). The unified
prop is `widget` only.

**Contract 3 — Registry / extension.**
The registry is *open*: apps may register additional widget types, but
the canonical types are owned by AF.

```js
// in app code
import { registerWidget, getWidget } from '@agent-foundation/ui-react';
import { SprintProgressWidget } from './widgets/SprintProgressWidget';

registerWidget('openteam.sprint_progress', SprintProgressWidget);
```

### 2.3 Consumption Model

We pick the **monorepo workspace** model so that:
- AgentFoundation owns the source; downstream apps depend on it via
  a workspace link (`yarn workspaces` / `pnpm workspace`) or a
  published `@agent-foundation/ui-react` npm package.
- The Python `widget_protocol` constants are mirrored into
  `widgets/src/protocol/widgetTypes.js` by a small codegen step
  (`scripts/sync-widget-types.py`) run in CI to prevent drift.

For RankEvolve (which lives in a separate Atlassian package), the
library is consumed via the **published npm package** rather than a
workspace link. The package is published from AgentFoundation CI.

---

## 3. Component Classification Matrix

Legend:
- **PROMOTE** — move to `@agent-foundation/ui-react`, delete duplicates downstream.
- **CANONICALIZE** — already in AF; reconcile divergence with RE/OS into one true version.
- **LIFT-AND-GENERALIZE** — exists in RE/OS in a domain-specific form; extract the generic shape.
- **KEEP-IN-APP** — domain-specific, stays in the consuming app.
- **DELETE** — duplicate or dead code.

### 3.1 Input widgets (chat-widgets / widgets)

| Component | OpenStartup | RankEvolve | AgentFoundation | Decision | Notes |
|-----------|-------------|------------|-----------------|----------|-------|
| TextInputWidget | `chat-widgets/TextInputWidget.js` | `widgets/TextInputWidget.js` (differs) | `widgets/TextInputWidget.js` | **CANONICALIZE** | Reconcile to one impl. AF version is base; pull "view file" affordance from OS. |
| SingleChoiceWidget | `chat-widgets/SingleChoiceWidget.js` | `widgets/SingleChoiceWidget.js` (differs) | `widgets/SingleChoiceWidget.js` | **CANONICALIZE** | OS has nice rich-vs-simple split; merge it in. |
| MultipleChoiceWidget | `chat-widgets/MultipleChoiceWidget.js` | `widgets/MultipleChoiceWidget.js` | `widgets/MultipleChoiceWidget.js` | **CANONICALIZE** | Already aligned; preserve `show_select_all` / `select_all_text` from `input_modes.py`. |
| ConfirmationWidget | `chat-widgets/ConfirmationWidget.js` | `widgets/ConfirmationWidget.js` (differs) | `widgets/ConfirmationWidget.js` | **CANONICALIZE** | Keep `metadata.view` / `metadata.view_type` callbacks; pull OS's optional "additional instructions" textarea. |
| DropdownWidget | (not present) | (not present) | `widgets/DropdownWidget.js` | **PROMOTE** | Already in AF; promote unchanged. |
| ToggleWidget | (not present) | (not present) | `widgets/ToggleWidget.js` | **PROMOTE** | Already in AF; promote unchanged. |
| ToolArgumentFormWidget | (not present) | (not present) | `widgets/ToolArgumentFormWidget.js` | **PROMOTE** | Already in AF; promote unchanged. |
| MultiInputWidget | (CompoundWidget inline in ConversationToolWidget) | `widgets/MultiInputWidget.js` | `widgets/MultiInputWidget.js` (differs) | **CANONICALIZE** | Unify the two MultiInput impls; absorb the OS CompoundWidget into it. |
| GroupedWidget | (not present) | `widgets/GroupedWidget.js` | (not present) | **LIFT-AND-GENERALIZE** | Plan v3 compound pattern; remove RE-specific "group resolve" semantics, keep generic stack. |
| ApprovalWidget | `chat-widgets/ApprovalWidget.js` | (not present) | (not present) | **PROMOTE** | Generic approve/reject; add `'approval'` to `widget_protocol.py` constants. |
| ChoiceWidget | `chat-widgets/ChoiceWidget.js` | (not present) | (not present) | **PROMOTE** | Card-style single-pick UI; rename `'card_choice'` to distinguish from radio `'single_choice'`. |
| DefaultWidget | (not present) | (not present) | `widgets/DefaultWidget.js` | **PROMOTE** | Fallback for unknown types. |
| ChatWidgetRenderer | `chat-widgets/ChatWidgetRenderer.js` | (inline in ChatMessage) | (none — uses registry directly) | **CANONICALIZE** | Promote OS's explicit renderer; thin wrapper over `getWidget(type)`. |
| ConversationToolWidget | `chat-widgets/ConversationToolWidget.js` | (different code paths) | (none) | **PROMOTE** | Generic `input_mode`-protocol dispatcher; the right place to centralize `input_mode.mode` → widget mapping. |
| WidgetRegistry | `chat-widgets/WidgetRegistry.js` (subset) | `widgets/WidgetRegistry.js` (differs) | `widgets/WidgetRegistry.js` (canonical-leaning) | **CANONICALIZE** | AF version is the closest to ideal; merge in OS's `'press_to_continue'` alias. |
| ToolConfigPanel | (not present) | `widgets/ToolConfigPanel.js` (differs) | `widgets/ToolConfigPanel.js` | **CANONICALIZE** | Generic; reconcile divergence. |
| ProposalSelectionWidget | (not present) | `widgets/ProposalSelectionWidget.js` | (not present) | **KEEP-IN-APP** | RE-specific proposals/phases/metrics. |
| ProjectSummaryWidget | `chat-widgets/ProjectSummaryWidget.js` | — | — | **KEEP-IN-APP** | OpenTEAM project domain. |
| SprintProgressWidget | `chat-widgets/SprintProgressWidget.js` | — | — | **KEEP-IN-APP** | OpenTEAM sprint domain. |
| TaskAssignmentWidget | `chat-widgets/TaskAssignmentWidget.js` | — | — | **KEEP-IN-APP** | OpenTEAM task assignment. |
| TaskListWidget | `chat-widgets/TaskListWidget.js` | — | — | **KEEP-IN-APP** | OpenTEAM task list. |
| WorkloadChartWidget | `chat-widgets/WorkloadChartWidget.js` | — | — | **KEEP-IN-APP** | OpenTEAM workload chart. |

