### 7.2 Code deliverables

- [ ] `widgets/` package skeleton with `package.json`, `src/`,
      `tests/`, `stories/`.
- [ ] All PROMOTE / CANONICALIZE components migrated.
- [ ] `widget_protocol.py` extended with new constants and a
      `WIDGET_TYPES` tuple.
- [ ] `scripts/sync_widget_types.py` (Py → JS codegen).
- [ ] `scripts/check_no_duplicate_widgets.py` (drift detector).
- [ ] OpenStartup `shared/` reduced to thin re-exports + 1–2
      app-specific files.
- [ ] RankEvolve `webui/react/src/components/widgets/` reduced to
      RE-specific widgets + re-exports.
- [ ] AgentFoundation `webui/react/src/components/widgets/` reduced
      to re-exports only.
- [ ] Snapshot/Storybook tests for every promoted component.

### 7.3 Acceptance criteria (overall)

1. Each of the three apps builds and runs visually unchanged.
2. `grep -rE "from '.*chat-widgets/(TextInput|SingleChoice|MultipleChoice|Confirmation|Approval|Choice)Widget'"` in OpenStartup returns **zero matches** (other than the re-export shim).
3. `grep -rE "from '.*shared/(EmptyState|LoadingIndicator|PersonChip|ProgressBar|QuickLinkButton|SectionCard|StatusBadge)'"` in OpenStartup returns **zero matches** (other than the re-export shim).
4. `diff -rq widgets/src/inputs/ <consumer>/widgets/` shows that no widget file exists in any consumer that isn't a one-line re-export.
5. `python scripts/check_widget_protocol_consistency.py` passes (Python ↔ JS type table identical).
6. CI is green in all three repos.

